# PART 3: SCAN PLANT SYSTEM

Create one dedicated and fully functional Scan Plant section.

All image-upload and camera functionality must exist only inside this section.

## 3.1 Two Image Upload Methods

Present two clear options.

### Option A: Multiple Images

Provide one upload area where users can:

- Select multiple images in a single file-selection operation.
- Drag and drop multiple images.
- Preview selected images.
- Remove unwanted images before analysis.
- Upload multiple images together.
- Submit the images for analysis.

Allow all image formats supported by the application and validate file types, sizes and content securely.

### Option B: Individual Plant Views

Allow users to upload images separately under three categories:

1. Front View
2. Back View
3. Close-up of Diseased Area

Users must be able to upload these images in any order.

Each category must have its own upload and preview area.

Do not force users to upload all three images if they only have one or two available. Allow submission with partial uploads, but communicate when additional views would improve diagnosis.

## 3.2 Camera Support

Provide one camera option inside the Scan Plant section.

Users should be able to:

- Open their device camera.
- Capture a plant image.
- Preview the captured image.
- Retake or remove it.
- Add captured images to the selected upload workflow.

Handle camera permissions and unsupported devices gracefully.

## 3.3 Automatic Analysis

After the user submits the images:

- Analyse the uploaded images automatically.
- Identify the plant or crop where supported.
- Detect possible disease or visible plant-health problems.
- Estimate prediction confidence.
- Identify visible symptoms.
- Estimate severity where supported.
- Generate a useful diagnosis report.

Do not require users to manually select a disease or choose from a large crop list.

If the model cannot identify the plant or disease reliably, communicate that clearly and recommend expert verification.

## 3.4 Empty State Before Analysis

Before image analysis:

- Plant name must be empty.
- Disease name must be empty.
- Confidence must be empty.
- Symptoms must be empty.
- Causes must be empty.
- Severity must be empty.
- Treatment must be empty.

Do not show pre-filled, fabricated or example diagnosis results as if they belong to the user.

Only populate diagnosis information after actual image analysis.

